// A BLANKET BOUND OVER A PACKAGE-LOCAL HOMONYM TRAIT.
//
// `Hash` is the collision: `logos.lang.hash::Hash` owns the bare registry slot,
// so THIS package's `Hash` is filed under `trait_ident_homonym_bound::Hash`
// (B-mv-02). Mono now keys its impl facts by that IDENTITY
// (impl_keys::CANONICAL_TRAIT → Mono::concrete_impls_, a pair), while a BOUND
// still reaches mono as bare TEXT. This file is the shape where those two meet.
//
// ⚠ WHAT THIS FILE IS NOT. It was written to be the SENSOR for mono.cpp's
// bare-spelling alias insert, and it is NOT one — MEASURED, both arms: with
// the alias disabled it is still green, because sema (not mono's fact table)
// decides which concretes a blanket admits. An earlier attempt, a plain
// generic bound `fn tag_of<T: Hash>(x: T) -> i64 { x.tag() }`, was likewise
// green with the alias off. The alias survives as a behaviour-preserving
// hedge with no witness, and mono.cpp says so at the insert. Do not cite this
// file as evidence that the alias is load-bearing.
//
// ⚠ WHAT IT DID EXPOSE, AND WHY THE BLANKET BODY DOES NOT CALL `tag()`. The
// bound is conflated on the SEMA side: `impl<T: Hash> Marker for T` admits the
// stdlib `Hash`'s concretes (`i32`, `i64`, …) into `Marker` as well as this
// package's `S`. With the body written as `return self.tag();` this program
// dies at `'func.call' op 'i32__tag' does not reference a valid function` — an
// MLIR verifier failure, not a diagnostic — and it does so with mono's alias
// ON *and* OFF, which is what locates the defect in sema. Canonicalising bound
// trait names at emit is what closes it; that is not this slice, and this file
// deliberately does NOT assert the defect as an expectation.
//
// What it therefore pins, and it is worth pinning: with the fact table keyed
// by trait identity, a package-local homonym trait still carries a working
// blanket and its own impl still dispatches. A canonicalisation that dropped
// the local trait's facts entirely would red here.
package trait_ident_homonym_bound;

extern fn printf(fmt: *const u8, ...) -> i32;
fn printi(fmt: str, v: i32) { unsafe { printf(fmt.as_ptr(), v); } }

pub trait Hash { fn tag(&self) -> i64; }

pub struct S { pub a: i32, }
impl Hash for S { fn tag(&self) -> i64 { return 91i64; } }

pub trait Marker { fn m(&self) -> i64; }
impl<T: Hash> Marker for T { fn m(&self) -> i64 { return 91i64; } }

fn call_marker<U: Marker>(x: U) -> i64 { return x.m(); }

fn main() -> i32 {
    let v: i64 = call_marker(S { a: 1i32 });
    let d: i64 = S { a: 1i32 }.tag();
    printi("tag=%d\n", v as i32);
    printi("direct=%d\n", d as i32);
    if v != 91i64 { return 41; }
    if d != 91i64 { return 42; }
    return 0i32;
}
